## 9. Frequently asked questions

| Q | A |
|---|---|
| **Do I still need a glyph server for Latin text?** | No. The `font-faces` entry for *Noto Sans Regular* will be used for all Latin code-points. The dummy `glyphs` URL is never hit. |
| **What if I want to keep a small glyph-PBF for a few icons (e.g. road shields) but otherwise use local fonts?** | You can keep the real `glyphs` URL pointing at a tiny server that only serves the ranges you need (e.g. `0-255.pbf`). The engine will request those ranges; everything else will fall back to `font-faces`. |
| **Can I use system fonts (e.g., Android’s built-in Roboto) without bundling a file?** | Yes – use the name `"Roboto"` in `text-font` and **do not** declare a `font-faces` entry for it. The native HarfBuzz engine will resolve the system font automatically. However, this makes the map style non-portable to other platforms (iOS, Web) where the same system font may not exist. |
| **My CJK labels look blocky / low-resolution. Why?** | Make sure you are loading the **OTF** version of the Noto CJK font (it contains the full SDF-compatible glyph outlines). The TTF version is larger but still works; the visual quality issue usually comes from using a *bitmap* fallback (e.g., the device’s default “sans-serif”). |
| **I get “Unable to load glyph range …” in Logcat. Is that a problem?** | Not for the offline case. The SDK tried to fetch a PBF because the `glyphs` URL exists, failed (404), and then fell back to the `font-faces` font. As long as the label appears correctly, you can ignore the warning or point `glyphs` at an empty folder to silence it. |
| **Do I need to call `map.setRTLTextPlugin()`?** | **No** – native RTL shaping is built-in from v11.13.0 onward. The plugin is only for old Mapbox GL JS versions. |
| **Can I change the font at runtime (e.g., user selects a different theme)?** | Yes. After the map is loaded, call `style.setFontFaces(newMap)` with a new mapping, then call `style.update()` (or just rely on the automatic refresh). The change is applied to all subsequent label draws. |

